{"type": "FeatureCollection", "metadata": {"note": "Henry Plant's counterpart to Flagler's Florida East Coast Railway (see florida_east_coast_railway.geojson) on Florida's Gulf coast. Plant opened the Waycross Short Line from Waycross, GA to Jacksonville in 1881, then in 1883 bought 60% of the South Florida Railroad, extending it from Sanford to Tampa (reached 1884) and on to Port Tampa (1888) to connect with his own steamship lines to Cuba. By 1900 this gave Florida's Gulf coast through rail service from the north, complementing the Atlantic-coast FEC. Plant died in 1899; his heirs sold the whole Plant System to the Atlantic Coast Line Railroad on July 1 1902. The Jacksonville-Sanford segment specifically was NOT built by Plant himself: it was a separate company, the Jacksonville, Tampa and Key West Railway (JT&KW), which only joined the Plant System in 1899. JT&KW built Jacksonville-Palatka first (construction began March 1883, regular service March 1884), then extended Palatka-Sanford in 1885 using the Palatka and Indian River Railway's right-of-way -- crossing the St. Johns River a few miles south of Palatka, running down its east bank past Pierson to the north edge of Lake Monroe, then crossing back over the river into Sanford, where it met the (Plant-controlled) South Florida Railroad; regular Sanford service began Feb 1886. Geometry is a real-town waypoint approximation (Waycross-Jacksonville-Palatka-Pierson-DeLand-Sanford-Kissimmee-Tampa-Port Tampa), straight-line segments between documented stations -- NOT digitized from period track maps.", "sources": ["https://www.frrm.org/history/ and https://metrojacksonville.com/mobile/article/2015-jul-henry-b-plant-the-king-of-florida (Waycross Short Line 1881; Plant Investment Company formed 1882, headquartered in Sanford; South Florida Railroad 60% stake purchased 1883; Port Tampa hotel/steamship connection 1888)", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Florida_Railroad (Sanford-Tampa line)", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacksonville,_Tampa_and_Key_West_Railway (Jacksonville-Palatka built 1883-84; Palatka-Sanford extension 1885 via the Palatka and Indian River Railway's right-of-way, crossing the St. Johns River twice en route to Sanford; regular Sanford service Feb 1886; JT&KW joined the Plant System in 1899)", "https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=135696 (Pierson Depot historical marker, confirming Pierson as a stop on this line)", "https://www.trains.com and https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant_System (Atlantic Coast Line absorbed the Plant System July 1 1902, following Plant's 1899 death)"], "not_yet_sourced": "Exact year the South Florida Railroad's Sanford-Tampa segment itself opened versus when Plant acquired it; precise frequency for any era, all estimated; whether ACL continued this route under a specific named train (e.g. a west-coast counterpart to the Champion) after 1902; whether the pre-1899 JT&KW segment should really be split out as its own feature/company rather than folded into the 'Plant System' label from 1884.", "line_label_audit": "2026-08-24: line labels normalised repo-wide to \"<operating company>: <line name>\" -- the company's common display name (legal suffixes dropped), then the line as a passenger would have known it, or its two terminals where the line carried no advertised name. Long intermediate station lists were reduced to endpoints. For features spanning several operators the company shown is the one that ran the line for most of its drawn years. See CLAUDE.md Rule 6."}, "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Plant System (South Florida Railroad / Jacksonville, Tampa and Key West Railway)", "line": "Plant System: Waycross \u2013 Port Tampa", "id": "plant-system-waycross-tampa", "color": "#CA6702", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 40, "speed_source": "estimated: 1880s-90s steam-era construction-stage railroad; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1884, "end": 1902, "headway_min": 480, "note": "Waycross Short Line opened 1881; South Florida Railroad (60% acquired by Plant 1883) reached Tampa 1884, extended to Port Tampa 1888 for steamship connections to Cuba; frequency estimated/unsourced", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://www.frrm.org/history/", "https://metrojacksonville.com/mobile/article/2015-jul-henry-b-plant-the-king-of-florida", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Florida_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacksonville", "https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=135696", "https://www.trains.com", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant_System"]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-81.6376, 29.6516], "to": [-81.4593, 29.2258], "chord_mi": 31.33, "traced_mi": 44.95, "snap_m": [205, 229], "bridged_mi": 0.33, "osm_lines": ["Sanford Subdivision (38.73 mi)", "Palatka-Lake Butler State Trail [abandoned] (1.74 mi)", "CSX Transportation (1.44 mi)", "Southern [abandoned] (0.81 mi)", "(rail) (0.8 mi)", "(abandoned) [abandoned] (0.72 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m; 0.33 mi bridged across gaps in OSM"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-81.2781, 28.8028], "to": [-81.4076, 28.2919], "chord_mi": 36.15, "traced_mi": 39.53, "snap_m": [44, 110], "bridged_mi": 0.54, "osm_lines": ["Central Florida Rail Corridor (37.94 mi)", "Goldsboro Pedestrian and Bike Trail [abandoned] (0.87 mi)", "(?) (0.54 mi)", "CSX Transportation (0.17 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m; 0.54 mi bridged across gaps in OSM"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-81.4593, 29.2258], "to": [-81.3031, 29.0283], "chord_mi": 16.58, "traced_mi": 21.12, "snap_m": [229, 372], "bridged_mi": 0.53, "osm_lines": ["Sanford Subdivision (16.65 mi)", "Deland Spur (3.22 mi)", "(?) (0.53 mi)", "C